---
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';
import ExternalLink from '../components/ExternalLink.astro';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';
import { breadcrumbLd } from '../lib/seo';

const description =
  'What While We Were There collects (almost nothing), how YouTube embeds work, and how to reach us about privacy.';
---

<Base
  title="Privacy policy"
  description={description}
  jsonLd={[
    breadcrumbLd([
      { name: 'Home', href: '/' },
      { name: 'Privacy policy', href: '/privacy/' },
    ]),
  ]}
>
  <PageHero
    eyebrow={`Last updated ${site.policyUpdated}`}
    title="Privacy policy"
    dek="This is a family website. The notes below describe what we actually do with this site, not a pile of clauses we copied from somewhere else."
    crumbs={[
      { name: 'Home', href: '/' },
      { name: 'Privacy policy', href: '/privacy/' },
    ]}
  />
  <div class="wrap stack">
    <section aria-labelledby="who-title">
      <h2 id="who-title">Who we are</h2>
      <p>
        While We Were There is a journal kept by Andrew and Michelle, with Harrison, Sullivan, and Maeve, in
        Toronto, Canada. The public site uses first names only. For a privacy question, email
        <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>.
      </p>
    </section>
    <section aria-labelledby="collect-title">
      <h2 id="collect-title">What this website collects</h2>
      <p>
        The site is a set of static pages. There are no accounts, no comments, no newsletter, and no analytics
        script. We do not ask you to sign in, and we do not set cookies of our own.
      </p>
      <p>
        When your browser loads a page, the company that hosts the site can record ordinary server data: an IP
        address, the date, the page address, and the browser name. That is part of running a web server. We do
        not add our own tracking on top, and we do not sell that information or use it to build a profile of
        you. The host is Hostinger. Their privacy policy is at
        <ExternalLink href="https://www.hostinger.com/legal/privacy-policy">hostinger.com/legal/privacy-policy</ExternalLink>.
      </p>
    </section>
    <section aria-labelledby="email-title">
      <h2 id="email-title">Email</h2>
      <p>
        If you email {site.email}, the message goes through your email app to our inbox. It is not stored by
        this website, because the website never receives it. Please do not send sensitive information, and
        please do not send a child's contact details, a surname, a school, or a home address.
      </p>
    </section>
    <section aria-labelledby="youtube-title">
      <h2 id="youtube-title">YouTube</h2>
      <p>
        Links to our channel, <ExternalLink href={site.youtube}>youtube.com/@Whilewewerethere</ExternalLink>,
        leave this site. YouTube then handles the visit under its own policy:
        <ExternalLink href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">policies.google.com/privacy</ExternalLink>.
      </p>
      <p>
        If a story includes a film, the player is not loaded with the page. It loads only after you press play,
        and it uses YouTube's privacy-enhanced domain (youtube-nocookie.com). After that, YouTube receives the
        request, including your IP address, under its own rules. You can always use the plain link and watch on
        YouTube instead.
      </p>
    </section>
    <section aria-labelledby="cookies-title">
      <h2 id="cookies-title">Cookies</h2>
      <p>
        We do not set cookies, and we do not use a cookie banner to announce cookies we are not setting. If you
        press play on an embedded film, YouTube may set cookies. If we later add advertising, this section will
        be rewritten before those ads go live, because an ad network would be a real change.
      </p>
    </section>
    <section aria-labelledby="children-title">
      <h2 id="children-title">Children</h2>
      <p>
        This journal is written by adults about our family. It is not a service for children to join. We do not
        knowingly collect personal information from children. The children are named by first name because the
        journal is theirs too. We do not publish a surname, a school, or a way to contact them.
      </p>
    </section>
    <section aria-labelledby="ads-title">
      <h2 id="ads-title">Ads and affiliate links</h2>
      <p>
        As of {site.policyUpdated}, we do not show ads and we do not use affiliate links. The design has a
        reserved place for both, and both are switched off, so published pages do not carry empty ad boxes or a
        disclosure about links that are not there.
      </p>
      <p>
        If that changes, this page will change in the same breath. Any story with an affiliate link will say so
        where you can see it. You would not pay more because of a commission. A commission would not be the
        reason we recommend something. A sponsored trip would be labeled as sponsored.
      </p>
    </section>
    <section aria-labelledby="changes-title">
      <h2 id="changes-title">Changes</h2>
      <p>
        If we change what this site does with information, we will update this page and the date at the top.
        The current version is dated {site.policyUpdated}.
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>
</Base>
